{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d0c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b1e-f583-7cc2-a513-9b90d8c833d2"},"sequence":1724,"recorded_at":1780531400003443,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8cd64a8a-faf9-439f-ae7d-60151e219433","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8cd64a8a-faf9-439f-ae7d-60151e219433","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8cd64a8a-faf9-439f-ae7d-60151e219433"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"6a7a7a56-9b4b-43dc-948a-53fd2b374609"},"task_id":"6a7a7a56-9b4b-43dc-948a-53fd2b374609","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"6a7a7a56-9b4b-43dc-948a-53fd2b374609","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-56-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -n 20 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===; git status --short | head -n 30; echo ===; git status --short | grep \\\"^??\\\" | head; echo ===; ls *.log *.tmp *.bak 2>&1 | head -n 5\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook tail and worktree cleanliness\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 5: B4/B5 closed as classes by derived denominators, N8 indirection refused\\n- FIX (B8): `bound_census_test.go` rosters all 97 production bound sites (six helpers by member, len guards by shape with values normalized out, DecodeFindings cap instantiations): 82 driven at entries both edges, 15 exempt (4 mechanism, 4 plumbing, 3 equivalent, 5 stated-bound 65536-count rows). `requireStringBounds`/`requireUint53Bounds` wrappers are mechanism rows; the 19 caller sites carry the rows.\\n- FIX (B7): `identity_census_test.go` rosters all 62 `X != Y` gates (mechanical classes excluded) plus a 5-row presence census with structural proof: 54 driven zero-on-exempted-side at exported entries (CheckProbe x6 both sides, seal 8x2, admission key x5 entry+binding sides, binding caller-side x4), 8 exempt (2 dispatch, 4 sentinel, 2 equivalent).\\n- FIX (N8): `constructorSitesInFile` reports any `axerror.New` selector outside call-fun position; synthetic proof covers package-level and function-local indirection (report) vs definition spelling and Decode (exempt).\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): `Bext-min` is genuinely equivalent (no 2-char key satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar); `Iops-candidate` is genuinely equivalent (both sides come from `requireDigestValue`); registry-element gates had no \\\"\\\" row (added `TestRegistryElementEmptyRefuses`); `Ituple-strategies` needed a struct-level [\\\"\\\"] row (added); `Ibind-tuple` first exempted the wrong side (context is never zero; corrected to the admitted side and killed). Len-guard census IDs briefly embedded values and caught a mutant statically — normalized to shape-only so values are pinned behaviorally, per the file's own documented design.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/battery.py`, 153 mutants applied by exact string, PRESENT-confirmed, restore-verified: 147 killed, 6 equivalent-confirmed (3 full-green, 3 behavioral-green with only the roster failing closed on the added clause), 0 survived, 0 not-applied. Additive probe file failed all three censuses naming the planted sites, then removed. Full table attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev5.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`bound_census_test.go`, `identity_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `zero_absent_test.go`); zero production changes, so no resurrections possible. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-cover` green (sessadapter 82.4%), `-race` green on the package, vet + gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n===\\n M LOGBOOK.md\\n M internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go\\n M internal/dirnode/decode.go\\n M internal/dirnode/probe.go\\n M internal/dirnode/query.go\\n M internal/environ/census_test.go\\n M internal/environ/decode.go\\n M internal/environ/decode_unit_test.go\\n M internal/environ/frame_agreement_test.go\\n M internal/environ/shape_census_test.go\\n M internal/environ/tuple_agreement_test.go\\n M internal/provhost/opdecode.go\\n M internal/provhost/protocol_test.go\\n M internal/sessadapter/bound_census_test.go\\n M internal/sessadapter/decode.go\\n M internal/sessadapter/identity_census_test.go\\n M internal/sessadapter/manifest.go\\n M internal/sessadapter/probe.go\\n M internal/sessadapter/tuple.go\\n?? internal/dirnode/rawuint53_test.go\\n?? internal/environ/census_audit_test.go\\n?? internal/environ/refusal_site_audit_test.go\\n?? internal/environ/scalar_agreement_test.go\\n?? internal/provhost/rawuint53_test.go\\n?? internal/sessadapter/rawuint53_test.go\\n===\\n?? internal/dirnode/rawuint53_test.go\\n?? internal/environ/census_audit_test.go\\n?? internal/environ/refusal_site_audit_test.go\\n?? internal/environ/scalar_agreement_test.go\\n?? internal/provhost/rawuint53_test.go\\n?? internal/sessadapter/rawuint53_test.go\\n===\\nls: *.bak: No such file or directory\\nls: *.log: No such file or directory\\nls: *.tmp: No such file or directory\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7658,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1915,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
